    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 276 tests pass. \n\nI implemented the change in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n- Added a `canonicalCity(...)` helper that, when an owner is created, checks whether any existing owner already lives in the same city (matched case- and whitespace-insensitively via the existing `normalize` method). If so, it reuses that owner's exact spelling; otherwise it title-cases the supplied city.\n- Added a `titleCase(...)` helper that upper-cases the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest (e.g. `\"new york\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`).\n- `owner.setCity(canonicalCity(owner.getCity()))` is called before duplicate checks, `customerCode` generation, and saving, so the canonical value is what gets persisted and returned in the `city` field.\n\nThe full suite (276 tests) is green.",
